    "narrative": "Today\u2019s offensive engine is anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who commands the highest score of the day (82.05). Despite facing a tough arm in Rod\u00f3n, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a prime #2 spot and a slight platoon advantage that keeps his efficiency ceiling high. We are also leaning heavily into the matchup against Crow, where **Luis Arraez** (69.53), **Jung Hoo Lee** (67.27), and **Matt Chapman** (64.59) all find themselves in strong territory. The massive +19% boost provided by the SP skill projection for Crow turns this bottom-tier starter into a high-leverage target for our middle-of-the-order bats, maximizing our potential in R, RBI, and AVG. Meanwhile, **Bryson Stott** (72.63) represents our secondary tier of elite starts; the combination of a generous matchup against Giolito and a strong dynamic platoon adjustment makes him a mandatory plug-in for our MI slot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved evaluating our lower-ceiling options against the risk of the day. **Geraldo Perdomo** (55.28) remains our most marginal start, falling into the \"cautionary\" zone as he faces Wrobleski. While **Geraldo Perdomo**\u2019s ability to swipe bags is vital for our pursuit of the stolen base category, his projected efficiency barely cleared the threshold for a start. We are closely monitoring the lineup pending status for **Will Smith**, whose 61.69 score assumes a #7 spot; if he shifts further down the order, we may see his efficiency degrade rapidly. Elsewhere, **Gavin Sheets** (46.45) is a pure punt play against Wheeler; he remains in the lineup purely to maintain plate appearance depth, but the -19% SP skill penalty suggests he is the most likely candidate to be pulled if we were to pinch hit for better late-game matchups.\n\nWe are navigating significant attrition with **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** both locked on the IL, while **Lawrence Butler** and **Tyler Freeman** remain unavailable due to roster status or scheduling. Our depth options like **Daulton Varsho**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Masyn Winn**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, and **Gleyber Torres** are currently sidelined, but we are keeping a close watch on them to cycle into the rotation should any of today\u2019s starters\u2014particularly **Gavin Sheets** or **Geraldo Perdomo**\u2014fail to produce early. The priority remains protecting our daily efficiency while ensuring we don't bleed too much value against elite arms like Wheeler, who represents the primary roadblock to a high-scoring day for the LawDog lineup.",
